==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*5 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 30~50 seconds<sup>900f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 60~100 seconds<sup>1,800f~3,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Super Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The combination of Metals and Shields appears to be a force to be reckoned with, but end up changing little aside from necessitating the use of [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critical Hitters]] and [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]]. The Metals even end up making this stage easier by enabling the use of [[Long Distance]] units to snipe Fallen Bear. Shield Piercers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]] greatly speed up this stage, as most of Fallen Bear's health pool is concentrated in his [[Shield]]. For Critical Hitters, [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] and [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] work exceptionally well here due to their high range. [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] is especially useful due to having both abilities. It is recommended to have at least a level 25 Seal before attempting this stage.

